## 🧩 MODULE 1 — Data Models (Lines 65–223)

### What is implemented

**`ExperienceItem` (Pydantic BaseModel)**
```
Fields:  company, role, duration_months (int, 0–600), responsibilities (list[str])
Config:  extra="forbid" — rejects any field the LLM hallucinated outside the schema
```
Two custom validators:
- `_coerce_duration` — converts string duration formats to int:
  - `"6 months"` → `6`, `"1 year"` → `12`, `"three"` → `3`
  - Has a word-to-number mapping: one, two, three ... twelve
  - Hard cap: `le=600` (50 years) — prevents hallucinated values like `360` months
- `_coerce_responsibilities` — accepts `None` or a plain string in place of a list

**`ParsedResume` (Pydantic BaseModel)**
```
Fields:  name (str), skills (list[str]), experience (list[ExperienceItem]), education (list[str])
Config:  extra="forbid"
```
Three custom validators:
- `_coerce_skills` — if LLM returns skills as a comma-string `"Python, Docker"`, splits it to `["Python", "Docker"]`
- `_strip_name` — strips whitespace, falls back to `"Unknown"` for blank/non-string
- `_deduplicate_skills` — removes duplicate skills case-insensitively, preserves insertion order

**`AnalysisResult` (Pydantic BaseModel)** — the full API response shape
```
Standard fields:   candidate_name, parsed_resume, total_score, matched_skills, missing_skills
Score breakdown:   semantic_skill_match (0–40), experience_longevity (0–35), context_alignment (0–25)
Processing meta:   extraction_tier_used, processing_time_ms, calibration_applied
Parse pipeline:    llm_parse_attempts, used_regex_fallback, difficult_layout_detected
                   manual_review_recommended, field_confidence, verified_skills
                   unverified_skills, unverified_fields
```

**`ParseResult` (Python dataclass)** — internal container between parsing and scoring
```
Fields:  resume (ParsedResume), llm_attempts (int), used_fallback (bool),
         field_confidence (dict), verified_skills, unverified_skills, unverified_fields
```

### What is NOT implemented / gaps

| Gap | Impact |
|---|---|
| No `projects` field in `ParsedResume` | Student projects are invisible to the system |
| No `certifications` field | Certifications are not tracked or scored |
| No `summary` or `objective` field | Profile summary is discarded |
| No `location` or `contact` fields | Cannot filter by geography |
| No `languages` field | Spoken languages ignored |
| Experience `duration_months` is an estimate | LLM can be wrong; no date parsing from raw text |

