## 🧩 MODULE 2 — PDF Text Extraction Pipeline (Lines 384–604)

### What is implemented

**Tier 1 — PyMuPDF (`_extract_tier1_fitz`)**
- Opens PDF from memory using `fitz.open(stream=..., filetype="pdf")`
- Uses `"blocks"` mode (not `"text"` mode) — extracts text WITH bounding-box spatial metadata
- Sorts blocks by `(round(y0/50)*50, x0)` — top-to-bottom then left-to-right
- This prevents two-column resumes from having left+right column text merged mid-sentence
- Returns combined page text

**Tier 2 — pdfplumber (`_extract_tier2_pdfplumber`)**
- Opens PDF from `io.BytesIO`
- Calls `page.extract_text(x_tolerance=3, y_tolerance=3)`
- Also calls `page.extract_tables()` — detected table cells serialized as `"col1 | col2 | col3"`
- Handles multi-column and table-heavy resumes

**Tier 3 — OCR (`_extract_tier3_ocr`)**
- Rasterizes each PDF page at **300 DPI** PNG using `pdf2image.convert_from_bytes`
- Uses custom OCR config: `--oem 3 --psm 6` (PSM 6 = uniform block of text — better for multi-column)
- Calls `pytesseract.image_to_string` per page
- **Per-page OCR confidence logging**: calls `image_to_data` to compute average confidence
  - Logs a WARNING if average confidence < 70%
  - Logs INFO otherwise
- Resolves Tesseract and Poppler paths dynamically:
  - Checks `TESSERACT_CMD` / `POPPLER_PATH` env vars first
  - Then checks system PATH (`shutil.which`)
  - Then checks hardcoded Windows paths as last resort

**Pipeline Orchestrator (`extract_text_pipeline`)**

Key upgrade over basic version:
- **Tier 1 and Tier 2 run CONCURRENTLY** using `asyncio.gather` + `run_in_executor`
  - This saves time — both run in parallel thread pool
- **Two-column layout detection**:
  - If Tier 2 yields 15%+ MORE content than Tier 1, Tier 2 is preferred
  - Rationale: if pdfplumber found significantly more, the resume likely had a multi-column layout that PyMuPDF merged
- If combined Tier1+Tier2 >= OCR_CHAR_THRESHOLD → returns combined, skips OCR
- OCR only triggered if both tiers together yield < 150 chars

### What is NOT implemented / gaps

| Gap | Impact |
|---|---|
| No DOCX / TXT support | Word document resumes rejected |
| No password-protected PDF detection | Encrypted PDFs silently return empty text |
| OCR confidence not exposed in API response | Frontend cannot warn user about low-quality extraction |
| No page count limit | A 200-page PDF would attempt full OCR |
| 150-char threshold hardcoded as a constant | Not adaptive — a 3-page resume with only 140 chars would still trigger OCR |
| Two-column detection is heuristic (15%) | Can misfire on resumes with wide margins |

