## 🧩 MODULE 6 — Experience Scoring (Lines 1418–1459)

### What is implemented

**Bracket system (`compute_experience_longevity`)**:
```
total_months = sum of all ExperienceItem.duration_months
has_skills_or_projects = bool(resume_skills) OR any(item.responsibilities for item in experience)

0 months, has skills/projects → 60% × 35 = 21.00 pts
0 months, nothing              → 40% × 35 = 14.00 pts
1–11 months                    → 75% × 35 = 26.25 pts
12–35 months                   → 90% × 35 = 31.50 pts
36+ months                     → 100% × 35 = 35.00 pts
```

Design rationale: Student-protective — someone with 0 months but strong skills should not score 0.

### What is NOT implemented / gaps

| Gap | Impact |
|---|---|
| Projects not counted as experience | A student with 5 strong projects gets same score as someone with nothing |
| Duration is LLM estimate, not calculated | If LLM hallucinates "24 months" for a 3-month internship, score inflates |
| No gap analysis | Career gaps not detected or flagged |
| No recency weighting | 4-year-old experience counts same as current |
| Experience relevance not checked | 10 years of cooking experience scores same as 10 years of software |

