## 🧩 MODULE 8 — API Endpoints (Lines 1477–1653)

### What is implemented

**`GET /`** — Serves `index.html` from the same directory as `main.py`

**`GET /health`** — Returns:
```json
{"status": "ok", "model": "llama-3.3-70b-versatile",
 "experience_target_months": 36, "api_key_configured": true}
```

**`POST /api/v1/analyze`** — Main endpoint:

Input validation order:
1. Content-type check (must be PDF or octet-stream)
2. Job description not empty
3. File read into memory (async)
4. File size check (0 bytes or > MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB)

Full processing pipeline:
1. PDF extraction (concurrent Tier1+Tier2, Tier3 if needed)
2. Sanitize raw text + job description
3. LLM parse with retry (up to 3 attempts + regex fallback)
4. Layout sanity check
5. Collect responsibilities
6. Skill match score (sync, CPU)
7. Experience score (sync, CPU)
8. Contextual score (async, second LLM call)
9. Aggregate + return AnalysisResult

All three scoring components are computed **sequentially** (not in parallel).

### What is NOT implemented / gaps

| Gap | Impact |
|---|---|
| No authentication (JWT, API key, session) | Open to anyone |
| No rate limiting | DoS vulnerability |
| No request ID / correlation ID | Cannot trace a specific request across logs |
| No database — all stateless | No history, no analytics, no comparison |
| Skill score + experience score computed before contextual LLM call — but not parallelized with it | Extra latency that could be reduced |
| No bulk/batch endpoint | Must analyze one resume at a time |
| No webhook or async callback | Client must wait synchronously for response |
| CORS allows all origins | No frontend restriction |

