## 🧩 MODULE 9 — Fairness Test Suite (`test_fairness.py`)

### What is implemented

12 deterministic regression tests, zero dependencies (no pytest, no API calls):

| Test ID | What it tests |
|---|---|
| FAIR-001 | Baseline: all skills matched, 36+ months → skill ≥ 38/40, exp = 35/35 |
| FAIR-002 | Empty education: scores identical to baseline (education not in scoring) |
| FAIR-003 | No certifications: scores identical to baseline |
| FAIR-004 | No projects: scores identical to baseline |
| FAIR-005 | Fresh grad, 0 months, has skills: exp = 21.0 (60% floor) |
| FAIR-006 | Fresh grad, 0 months, has responsibilities: same 21.0 floor |
| FAIR-007 | Completely empty: skill = 0.0, exp = 14.0 (40% floor), never negative |
| FAIR-008 | Partial skills (3/5): proportional score in [20.0, 28.0] |
| FAIR-009 | Alias equivalence: `React.js/Postgres/K8s` = `React/PostgreSQL/Kubernetes` |
| FAIR-010 | Empty responsibilities, 24 months: bracket = 90% (31.5) |
| FAIR-011 | No required skills: score = 0.0, not scored, not penalized |
| FAIR-012 | Missing certs + projects: total ≥ baseline − 0.01 |

Custom minimal test framework (no external dependencies): `_results` list + `_test()` function.

### What is NOT implemented / gaps

| Gap | Impact |
|---|---|
| Only 12 tests | Very shallow coverage |
| No tests for skill normalization edge cases | Alias resolution bugs won't be caught |
| No tests for LLM parsing | Cannot verify LLM output quality |
| No integration tests | No end-to-end API test |
| No PDF extraction tests | Cannot verify tier switching behavior |
| No security/injection tests | Cannot verify sanitizer is working |
| No performance tests | Cannot detect regressions in response time |

